+Looking at this issue, I can see the problem is in `pylint/reporters/text.py` in the `on_set_current_module` method.
+
+The current code uses a regex `r"\{(.+?)(:.*)?\}"` to find template arguments. With a template like `{{ "Category": "{category}" }}`, the regex matches from the *first* `{`, producing the bogus argument `{ "Category"` instead of correctly recognizing the escaped braces `{{`/`}}` and the real `{category}` field.
+
+## The fix
+
+Use the standard library's `string.Formatter().parse()`, which correctly understands `{{`/`}}` escaping, identifies the real replacement fields, and yields their literal / field-name / format-spec / conversion parts. I reconstruct the template, re-escaping the literal parts (so their braces survive `str.format`) and dropping only fields that aren't valid `Message` attributes.
+
+This keeps the existing behavior (warn + drop unknown fields, e.g. `{unknown_attr}`) while correctly handling escaped braces.
