+
+For the template from the issue, `{{ "Category": "{category}" }}`:
+
+- `string.Formatter().parse()` yields `('{ "Category": "', 'category', '', None)` and `('" }', None, None, None)` — i.e. it correctly treats `{{`/`}}` as escaped literal braces and only sees `category` as a field.
+- `category` is a valid `Message` field, so no warning is emitted and nothing is removed.
+- The literal parts are re-escaped back to `{{ "Category": "` and `" }}`, so `_fixed_template` is unchanged.
+- At output time, `_fixed_template.format(**self_dict)` renders `{ "Category": "convention" }` etc. — as expected.
